body:
Done in lap session S104 (L2984–L2997), git `44a70b9`. `SPEC-branches.md` now says:
- `.lap/lineage` (machine-local) names a folder's lineage; `branch start` writes it (step 6);
- an empty open chunk is not sealed again;
- the base is always the parent's head; files are checked against it; `not_clean` names its two usual causes; a first folder that only merges is the recommended layout;
- the `branch` record carries `base_chunk`, so a folder's history is whole chunks;
- ids repeat across folders: shared text cites hashes and `<branch>/S<n>`;
- `LAP_BRANCH` stands in for `--branch`;
- `lap merge` seals the branch's open chunk and copies its chunks when the folder is reachable (identical files for a later `git merge`; `from` links survive);
- adopted sessions: branch starts with none open, adopted starts/ends never touch the parent's active session, later merges extend the adopted session, messages copied unchecked;
- the effort-cap note; `nested_branch` out of scope; open question 1 settled.

T-107, T-109, T-112 carry comments with the changes.
